	  Tab	   : Options:LockTab / UnlockTab / SelectTab / AddTabDivider / ToggleSection (category arrow)
	  Window	: Options:Toggle / Destroy / SetToggleKey / Dialog
	  OpenButton: floating draggable open/close button -> CreateWindow({ OpenButton = {...} }), Options:EditOpenButton({...})

	Added in this version (WindUI parity, only what was missing):
	  Every element : :SetTitle(text) / :SetDesc(text) / :Lock() / :Unlock() / :IsLocked() / :Destroy()
	  Code          : :SetCode(text)   (AddCode now also supports Locked / Lock / Unlock / SetTitle / SetDesc)
	  Window        : :LockAll() / :UnlockAll() / :GetElements() / :GetLockedElements() / :GetUnlockedElements()
				  :Open() / :Close() / :IsOpen() / :OnOpen(fn) / :OnClose(fn) / :OnDestroy(fn)

	WindUI theming (colours, names and fallbacks are the same as WindUI):
	  Themes    : Dark, Light, Rose, Plant, Red, Indigo, Sky, Violet, Amber, Emerald, Midnight, Crimson, Monokai Pro, Cotton Candy, Mellowsi
	  Window    : CreateWindow({ Theme = "Rose" })   Options:SetTheme("Sky")   Options:GetThemes()   Options:GetCurrentTheme()
	  Custom    : Library:AddTheme({ Name = "Mine", Accent = "#..", Dialog = "#..", Text = "#..", Background = "#..", Button = "#..",
				  Icon = "#..", Placeholder = "#..", Toggle = "#..", Slider = "#..", Checkbox = "#..", Primary = "#.." })
				  (same as Options:AddTheme).  Colours may be hex strings or Color3.  Missing keys fall back to WindUI's Dark theme.
				  Primary missing -> the highlight follows Accent (or Button when Accent is too close to the background).  Outline = border colour.
				  CreateWindow({ Theme = { Accent = "#..", Background = "#.." } }) and Library:SetTheme({...}) also take a table directly.
	  Icons     : OpenButton / AddTab accept "rbxassetid://..", an asset id, or a Lucide name ("settings", "lucide:sword")

	Font            : CreateWindow({ Font = "rbxassetid://12187365364" })  Library:SetFont(...) / Window:SetFont(...)  (asset id, Enum.Font, Font or font name)
	Tab category    : Window:AddTabSection({ Name = "Main" }) has a title + arrow; Window:AddTabSection({}) has no title (just a gap).  Both return an object -> AddTab({ Section = Group }).  Divider = true adds a line (Group:SetDivider(bool))
	Hub name        : CreateWindow({ Title = "My Hub" })  Window:SetTitle("New name")  Window:GetTitle()  ShowTitle = false hides it
